# Plan v2 — beyond customer comments (2026-10-11)

Owner: agent session `ehl-munich-final-e3`, branch `feat/v2-multi-trigger` (worktree `.claude/worktrees/v2`, own DB copy).
Asked by Atahan, 2026-10-11. Inputs:
- BMW support's message on the annual report: market & sales data, product strategy & R&D.
- Atahan's review:
  - Customer feedback is the only real trigger.
  - Compliance and regulation are missing.
  - Public reviews across brands are missing.
  - There's no explanation of why Chinese brands are winning.
  - Customers aren't grouped.
  - Models aren't grouped.
  - There's no offering per market.

Decision numbers for this work: **D-040+**, questions **Q-026+** (the 3D-view session holds D-039 / Q-025).

## 1. Diagnosis (what the current system skips)

| BMW process box (image_2) | Today | Gap |
|---|---|---|
| Baseline: previous model | Verbatims + study on the predecessor | Option list (458 items) is ingested but never used to decide anything |
| Baseline: BMW portfolio | Platforms, plants (feasibility only) | No "what other BMW models / NK already have" as a trigger (carry-over, NK flow-down) |
| Baseline: sales volume | Market volume factor (stylized file) | Annual report T1 facts (regional growth, EV share, model-series trends) not in the DB |
| Competition | 47 competitor_advantage web findings, used only as scoring support | Competitors never *originate* a requirement |
| Customer / public feedback | BMW verbatims only | No public owner reviews, no cross-brand view |
| Product & global trends | 20 trend + 26 expectation findings | Trends never originate; 31/39 requirements are `today` |
| Structure: "all potential requirements (0/1)" | Requirements exist only if derived from clusters | No candidate catalogue with an explicit implement yes/no per derivative × market |
| Requirements definition: groups | Categories exist | Powertrain / Driver assistance thin (5 each) |
| Prioritization: Customer / Business / … | One blended score | No visible Customer vs Business split; no strategic alignment; no compliance dimension |

## 2. Pillars

Each pillar gets its own decision entry when built.

**P1 — Multi-trigger requirements (image_2 "Situation analysis").**
- Every requirement gets an `origin` (trigger lane): customer voice, competitor gap, trend / future need, BMW baseline & portfolio (predecessor option list, NK / OS X flow-down), strategy (annual report), regulation-driven.
- A **candidate catalogue** (the "0/1 list") is built from:
  - option lists;
  - a competitor feature matrix;
  - trends;
  - regulation.
- Each candidate gets an implement yes/no proposal per derivative × market, with its evidence. Candidates with a yes become requirements through the same derivation, linker, fit and scoring steps.
- The evidence mix per requirement is shown, e.g. "60 % customer voice, 25 % competitors, 15 % trends".

**P2 — Regulatory & compliance radar** (scope reconciliation, decision needed: D-040).
- BMW's brief puts regulatory *requirements* out of scope. Atahan wants compliance in. Reconciliation: regulation is **context, trigger and gate**, never an output spec.
  - (a) A `regulation` reference table: EU / US / CN, title, status, effective date, T1 source, customer-facing consequence. Examples to verify:
    - Euro NCAP 2026 physical controls;
    - China's 2027 door-handle rule;
    - China's L2 ADAS marketing / OTA rules;
    - EU GSR2 ISA / driver monitoring;
    - UN R155 / R156 OTA;
    - EU Data Act;
    - China data export rules.
  - (b) A `compliance` fit check per target: `pass` (no conflict) / `warn` (affected, needs adaptation) / `fail` (conflicts with binding regulation in that market).
  - (c) Regulation-triggered *customer-facing* requirements, e.g. "the most-used functions are reachable without touchscreen menus", not "comply with ECE R…".
  - (d) A Regulatory radar page.

**P3 — Customer groups and model groups.**
- Personas, for example:
  - driving purist / enthusiast;
  - digital-first;
  - comfort & chauffeur (China LWB rear seat);
  - family & practical;
  - status & design;
  - pragmatic EV switcher.
- Personas are evidence-backed: signal-level persona tags (cheap model), web / annual-report sources, and the persona mix per derivative × market.
- Model groups by segment, body, powertrain and platform (CLAR / FAAR → NK).
- Requirements carry the personas they serve. Priorities can be viewed per persona. Must-not-lose traits per persona (e.g. the enthusiast's steering feel) protect against "one average customer".

**P4 — Market offering strategy (variants & packages, in scope).**
- For configurable items (option-list items + catalogue candidates), propose per derivative × market one of: standard, package, optional, or don't offer.
- Factors:
  - rough price (option list, as effort proxy only — no business case);
  - market saturation (share of competitors with it as standard);
  - customer expectation (study, verbatims, persona mix);
  - competitive pressure.
- Shown as an offering matrix with a rationale per cell. Each row is a proposal for the PM.

**P5 — Public reviews and market intelligence.**
- Find aggregators of owner reviews and ratings across brands, for example:
  - NHTSA complaints API (US, official);
  - J.D. Power APEAL / IQS / China studies;
  - Autohome / Dongchedi owner ratings (CN);
  - Edmunds / Cars.com;
  - What Car?.
- Ingest only what's allowed and cite it.
- Combine with registration and sales data (CPCA, KBA / ACEA, US) for a **"why" analysis** per market:
  - why Chinese brands grow;
  - how BMW regains China share;
  - where BMW can grow in Europe;
  - US powertrain shift.
- Output: cited market-strategy findings (T1–T3) that feed the competitor and strategy lanes. Correlation is labelled as correlation, never as cause.

**P6 — Annual report as T1 evidence (BMW support's message).**
- Annual report facts become `source_item(kind=reference, T1)` with page numbers:
  - regional growth, model-series deliveries, EV share by region;
  - R&D priorities, NK, ConnectedDrive / My BMW App metrics.
- Used for:
  - market momentum (scoring);
  - strategic alignment (new factor: does the requirement ride an NK / OS X / R&D investment?);
  - personas (where BMW grows);
  - feasibility timing.

**P7 — Scoring v4: Customer vs Business vs Compliance** (image_2 prioritization).
- Two visible sub-scores:
  - **Customer value:** voice, satisfaction gap, persona reach, future relevance.
  - **Business value:** market volume and momentum, competitive pressure, strategic alignment, portfolio leverage, effort.
- **Compliance** is a gate or flag, not a weight.
- The final score stays explainable (waterfall). There's a Customer × Business 2×2 chart per market.

**P8 — Make it shine (UI).**
- New pages:
  - Market strategy (CN / EU / US story with charts);
  - Customer groups;
  - Offering matrix;
  - Regulatory radar;
  - Candidate catalogue (0/1);
  - Customer × Business matrix.
- Changes to existing pages: Home tells the multi-trigger story; Review shows origin, personas and compliance; the How-it-works page gains the new steps.
- Page registration in `app.py` is coordinated with the 3D session (it owns the PAGES block edits for its page).

**P9 — How loud vs. how big: self-selection and tone** (Atahan, 2026-10-11).
- **Self-selection:** unhappy customers write, happy ones mostly don't. Unprompted complaints overstate pain.
- **Voice-vs-study calibration** per topic × derivative × market. The customer study is the less self-selected sample.
  - Many complaints, but a study rating at or above average → `vocal_minority`: customer voice damped.
  - Weak study rating with few complaints → `silent_dissatisfaction`: boosted.
- **Channel bias:** each channel's like/complaint ratio (prompted surveys vs hotline notes). A complaint from a channel where people mostly praise counts more.
- **Public reviews** (owner ratings across brands) are less self-selected than complaint databases. Their tier and weight say so.
- **Tone:** a cheap-model pass adds per signal:
  - intensity 1–5;
  - impact (cosmetic / annoyance / workaround / can't use / safety-relevant);
  - loyalty risk (explicit churn or "never again").
- Tone replaces the flat low/medium/high severity weight in customer voice.
- Everything visible in the score waterfall ("loud but the study is fine → ×0.7"), never a hidden multiplier.

## 3. Phases

| Phase | What | Who | Paid? |
|---|---|---|---|
| A. Research (parallel) | A1 regulation radar · A2 public reviews + market intelligence (sources, endpoints, data) · A3 personas & model groups · A4 market offering (option list + competitor standard equipment) · A5 annual-report facts as structured JSON | 5 subagents → docs in `foundation/documents/` + JSON seeds in `data/seed/` | No OpenAI spend (Claude web tools) |
| B. Design | Schema v2 (origin, persona, regulation, compliance check, candidate, offering), scoring v4, decisions D-040+ | me | — |
| C. Build (parallel, file-partitioned) | ingest seeds · candidate catalogue + multi-lane derivation · persona tagging · offering engine · compliance check · scoring v4 · UI pages | subagents per module, I integrate | pilot first |
| D. Run | pilot → full rebuild of `wave1` / `demo` snapshots in the worktree DB | me | ≤ $20 (budget now $7.37) |
| E. Validate | tests, judge benchmark, browser walk-through, validation report | subagents + me | small |
| F. Merge | rebase on main, coordinate DB swap with the 3D session, foundation docs, commit when asked | me | — |

## 4. Guardrails

- AGENTS rules hold:
  - the PM decides;
  - append-only audit;
  - web facts need a URL, a date and a tier;
  - no LLM opinions stored as sources;
  - BMW raw data never leaves the machine, except to OpenAI.
- Regulation is never output as a homologation spec (D-040). Rough price is an effort proxy, never a business case.
- Scraping only where the terms allow it. Prefer official APIs and press releases. Store quotes, not whole pages.
"""SQLite store (D-016) with sqlite-vec loaded (D-018). Tables per D-021."""

import sqlite3
from pathlib import Path

import sqlite_vec

from bmw_req.config import get_settings

NOW = "(strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%fZ', 'now'))"

# Demo table set (D-021). JSON columns hold lists/objects; *_json columns are TEXT.
SCHEMA = f"""
-- Reference layer (portfolio) ------------------------------------------------
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS brand (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, brand_group TEXT, positioning TEXT,
    core_values_json TEXT, guardrails_json TEXT, source_ids_json TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS platform (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, owner_brand_group TEXT, powertrains_json TEXT, introduced TEXT,
    phase_out TEXT, successor_platform_id TEXT REFERENCES platform(id), source_ids_json TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS vehicle_model (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, brand_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES brand(id), line TEXT, body TEXT,
    segment TEXT, platform_id TEXT REFERENCES platform(id), generation TEXT, sop TEXT,
    eop_planned TEXT, powertrains_json TEXT, is_bmw_group INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    market_variants_json TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS market (
    code TEXT PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, countries_json TEXT NOT NULL,  -- ["*"] = catch-all
    climate TEXT, usage_patterns TEXT, cultural_expectations TEXT, infrastructure TEXT,
    powertrain_mix TEXT, profile_source_ids_json TEXT, profile_valid_from TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS plant (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, city TEXT, country TEXT, platforms_json TEXT,
    powertrains_json TEXT, nk_ready_from TEXT, capacity_note TEXT, source_ids_json TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS production (
    vehicle_model_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicle_model(id), plant_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES plant(id),
    market_variant TEXT, markets_served_json TEXT, since TEXT, until TEXT, source_ids_json TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS sales (
    vehicle_model_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicle_model(id), market_code TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES market(code),
    year INTEGER NOT NULL, units INTEGER, is_forecast INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    source_item_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES source_item(id)
);

-- Evidence layer ---------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS ingest_batch (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, ts TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW},
    kind TEXT NOT NULL,           -- feedback_wave | study | sales | option_list | competitor_event | web_refresh | reference
    description TEXT, file TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS source_item (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
    kind TEXT NOT NULL,           -- feedback | study | sales | option_list | web | reference
    ref TEXT NOT NULL,            -- provenance: e.g. 'G60_feedback_hackathon.xlsx#Feedback_Explorer:G60-0001'
    external_id TEXT,             -- e.g. verbatim ID G60-0001
    trust_tier TEXT,              -- T1..T3
    vehicle_model_id TEXT REFERENCES vehicle_model(id), market_code TEXT REFERENCES market(code),
    country TEXT, platform_id TEXT REFERENCES platform(id),
    url TEXT, published_at TEXT, retrieved_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW},
    text TEXT, quote TEXT, meta_json TEXT,
    ingest_batch_id INTEGER REFERENCES ingest_batch(id),
    UNIQUE (kind, ref)
);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ix_source_scope ON source_item(vehicle_model_id, market_code);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS finding (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, type TEXT, title TEXT NOT NULL, summary TEXT,
    scope_level TEXT,             -- derivative | platform | market | portfolio
    vehicle_model_id TEXT REFERENCES vehicle_model(id), market_code TEXT REFERENCES market(code),
    platform_id TEXT REFERENCES platform(id),
    metrics_json TEXT, created_by TEXT NOT NULL, created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW}
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS finding_source (
    finding_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES finding(id), source_item_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES source_item(id),
    quote TEXT, relation TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'supports',   -- supports | contradicts
    PRIMARY KEY (finding_id, source_item_id)
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS verbatim_extraction (   -- one row per verbatim × extractor version (D-022)
    source_item_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES source_item(id), extractor_version TEXT NOT NULL,
    in_scope INTEGER NOT NULL, out_of_scope_reason TEXT, llm_usage_id INTEGER REFERENCES llm_usage(id),
    recheck_llm_usage_id INTEGER REFERENCES llm_usage(id),   -- second-pass check of an out-of-scope verdict (D-023)
    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW},
    PRIMARY KEY (source_item_id, extractor_version)
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS signal (                -- AI-extracted customer signal; input to findings (D-022)
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, source_item_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES source_item(id),
    extractor_version TEXT NOT NULL, category TEXT NOT NULL, topic TEXT, feedback_type TEXT NOT NULL,
    severity TEXT, need_statement TEXT, quote TEXT,
    quote_verified INTEGER NOT NULL,   -- quote is a contiguous span of the verbatim (whitespace/case normalized)
    llm_usage_id INTEGER REFERENCES llm_usage(id),   -- call (and so model) that produced it (D-023)
    FOREIGN KEY (source_item_id, extractor_version) REFERENCES verbatim_extraction(source_item_id, extractor_version)
);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ix_signal_source ON signal(source_item_id);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS finding_signal (       -- cluster membership: which signals make up a finding (D-025)
    finding_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES finding(id), signal_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES signal(id),
    PRIMARY KEY (finding_id, signal_id)
);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS ix_finding_signal_signal ON finding_signal(signal_id);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS study_metric (           -- one row per study item × model × market (D-026)
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, source_item_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES source_item(id),
    vehicle_model_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicle_model(id), market_code TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES market(code),
    item TEXT NOT NULL,           -- category / question text as in the file
    scale TEXT NOT NULL,          -- mean_10 (CN/EU means) | dist_7 (US 7-point distribution)
    mean REAL, top2 REAL, bottom3 REAL, net REAL,
    z_within_column REAL,         -- standardized vs. the other items of the same model × market column
    rank_within_column INTEGER, n_items_in_column INTEGER
);

-- Decision layer ---------------------------------------------------------------
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS requirement (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,          -- REQ-0001
    title TEXT NOT NULL, description TEXT, category TEXT, target_metric TEXT, acceptance_criteria TEXT,
    horizon TEXT,                 -- today | at_successor_launch
    kano_class TEXT, kano_drift TEXT, evidence_level TEXT,   -- E1..E4
    assumptions TEXT, uncertainties TEXT, conflicting_evidence TEXT,
    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'proposed', version INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1,
    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW}
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS requirement_target (
    requirement_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES requirement(id),
    vehicle_model_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicle_model(id), market_code TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES market(code),
    realization TEXT,             -- carry_over | platform_wide | derivative_specific | market_variant | package
    score REAL, score_breakdown_json TEXT, priority TEXT, rationale TEXT,
    PRIMARY KEY (requirement_id, vehicle_model_id, market_code)
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS requirement_finding (
    requirement_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES requirement(id), finding_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES finding(id),
    relation TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'supports',
    PRIMARY KEY (requirement_id, finding_id)
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS fit_check (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, requirement_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES requirement(id),
    vehicle_model_id TEXT REFERENCES vehicle_model(id), market_code TEXT REFERENCES market(code),
    check_type TEXT NOT NULL,     -- brand | segment | market | feasibility
    result TEXT NOT NULL,         -- pass | warn | fail
    rationale TEXT, evidence_source_ids_json TEXT, checked_by TEXT NOT NULL, checked_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW}
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS audit_event (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, ts TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW},
    actor_type TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (actor_type IN ('ai', 'human', 'system')), actor_id TEXT,
    action TEXT NOT NULL, entity_type TEXT NOT NULL, entity_id TEXT NOT NULL,
    field TEXT, old_value TEXT, new_value TEXT, rationale TEXT, model TEXT, prompt_ref TEXT
);
CREATE TRIGGER IF NOT EXISTS audit_event_no_update BEFORE UPDATE ON audit_event
BEGIN SELECT RAISE(ABORT, 'audit_event is append-only'); END;
CREATE TRIGGER IF NOT EXISTS audit_event_no_delete BEFORE DELETE ON audit_event
BEGIN SELECT RAISE(ABORT, 'audit_event is append-only'); END;

-- Continuity layer (D-013) -----------------------------------------------------
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS weights_version (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, weights_json TEXT NOT NULL, created_by TEXT NOT NULL,
    created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW}, rationale TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS prioritization_run (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, ts TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW},
    trigger TEXT NOT NULL,        -- new_evidence | weight_change | pm_request | scheduled
    ingest_batch_id INTEGER REFERENCES ingest_batch(id), weights_version_id INTEGER REFERENCES weights_version(id),
    model TEXT, initiated_by TEXT NOT NULL
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS score_snapshot (
    run_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES prioritization_run(id), requirement_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES requirement(id),
    vehicle_model_id TEXT NOT NULL, market_code TEXT NOT NULL,
    score REAL, breakdown_json TEXT, rank INTEGER, priority TEXT,
    PRIMARY KEY (run_id, requirement_id, vehicle_model_id, market_code)
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS change_proposal (
    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, run_id INTEGER REFERENCES prioritization_run(id),
    requirement_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES requirement(id), vehicle_model_id TEXT, market_code TEXT,
    field TEXT NOT NULL, old_value TEXT, proposed_value TEXT, reason TEXT, evidence_delta_json TEXT,
    status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'open',   -- open | accepted | rejected
    decided_by TEXT, decided_at TEXT, decision_rationale TEXT
);

-- Situation analysis beyond customer comments (plan-v2, D-040+) ---------------------
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS persona (                 -- customer group (P3); evidence in source_ids_json
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, description TEXT, values_json TEXT, must_not_lose_json TEXT,
    deal_breakers_json TEXT, cues_json TEXT, models_json TEXT, source_ids_json TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS persona_weight (          -- persona mix per derivative × market (estimate or measured)
    vehicle_model_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicle_model(id), market_code TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES market(code),
    persona_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES persona(id), weight REAL NOT NULL,
    basis TEXT NOT NULL,          -- estimate | signals
    note TEXT,
    PRIMARY KEY (vehicle_model_id, market_code, persona_id, basis)
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS signal_persona (          -- which customer group a signal speaks for (embedding match)
    signal_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES signal(id), persona_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES persona(id),
    score REAL NOT NULL, method TEXT NOT NULL,
    PRIMARY KEY (signal_id, persona_id)
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS signal_tone (             -- how big a problem is, from the customer's tone (P9)
    signal_id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY REFERENCES signal(id),
    intensity INTEGER NOT NULL,   -- 1 mild remark … 5 furious / ecstatic
    impact TEXT NOT NULL,         -- praise | cosmetic | annoyance | workaround | cannot_use | safety
    loyalty_risk INTEGER NOT NULL,  -- explicit churn / "never again" / regret (pains); 0 otherwise
    loyalty_cue TEXT, version TEXT NOT NULL, llm_usage_id INTEGER REFERENCES llm_usage(id)
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS model_group (
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, description TEXT, members_json TEXT, personas_json TEXT,
    shared_needs_json TEXT, source_ids_json TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS regulation (              -- context, trigger and gate — never an output spec (D-040)
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, jurisdiction TEXT NOT NULL, title TEXT NOT NULL, instrument TEXT, status TEXT,
    dates_json TEXT, categories_json TEXT, consequence TEXT, opportunity TEXT, risk TEXT, models_json TEXT,
    trust_tier TEXT, source_ids_json TEXT, finding_id INTEGER REFERENCES finding(id)
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS candidate (               -- the "all potential requirements (0/1)" list (image_2)
    id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,          -- CAND-001
    title TEXT NOT NULL, description TEXT, category TEXT,
    origin TEXT NOT NULL,         -- customer_voice | competitor | trend | baseline | strategy | regulation | offering
    feature_id TEXT, finding_ids_json TEXT, personas_json TEXT,
    created_by TEXT NOT NULL, created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW}
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS candidate_target (
    candidate_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES candidate(id),
    vehicle_model_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicle_model(id), market_code TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES market(code),
    implement INTEGER,            -- AI proposal 1 / 0
    rationale TEXT, requirement_id TEXT REFERENCES requirement(id),
    PRIMARY KEY (candidate_id, vehicle_model_id, market_code)
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS offering (                -- per-market offer proposal for configurable features (P4)
    feature_id TEXT NOT NULL, vehicle_model_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES vehicle_model(id),
    market_code TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES market(code),
    feature_json TEXT,            -- name, category, price band, option codes
    recommendation TEXT NOT NULL, -- standard | package | optional | do_not_offer (AI proposal)
    confidence TEXT, rationale TEXT, factors_json TEXT, sources_json TEXT,
    decision TEXT,                -- PM decision (same values), NULL = open
    decided_by TEXT, decided_at TEXT, decision_rationale TEXT,
    PRIMARY KEY (feature_id, vehicle_model_id, market_code)
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS app_state (               -- e.g. current simulated wave (D-027)
    key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, value TEXT NOT NULL, updated_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW}
);

-- LLM bookkeeping (D-014, D-010) ----------------------------------------------
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS llm_usage (
    id                 INTEGER PRIMARY KEY,
    created_at         TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW},
    settled_at         TEXT,
    job                TEXT NOT NULL,
    demo               INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    kind               TEXT NOT NULL,            -- responses | embeddings
    model              TEXT NOT NULL,
    service_tier       TEXT,
    status             TEXT NOT NULL,            -- reserved | completed | failed
    reserved_usd       REAL NOT NULL,
    cost_usd           REAL,
    input_tokens       INTEGER,
    cached_tokens      INTEGER,
    cache_write_tokens INTEGER,
    output_tokens      INTEGER,
    reasoning_tokens   INTEGER,
    search_calls       INTEGER,
    response_id        TEXT,
    error              TEXT
);
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS llm_cache (
    key TEXT PRIMARY KEY,         -- sha256 of model + request
    job TEXT, model TEXT NOT NULL, created_at TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT {NOW},
    output_text TEXT, llm_usage_id INTEGER REFERENCES llm_usage(id)
);

-- Vectors (D-018): rowid = source_item.id -------------------------------------
CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE IF NOT EXISTS source_embedding USING vec0(embedding float[1536]);
-- rowid = signal.id (D-025): clustering into findings + semantic retrieval for PM challenges
CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE IF NOT EXISTS signal_embedding USING vec0(embedding float[1536]);
"""


def connect(path: Path | str | None = None) -> sqlite3.Connection:
    """Open the app DB (default `data/app.db`), load sqlite-vec and ensure the schema.

    Autocommit mode: callers open transactions explicitly (`BEGIN IMMEDIATE`).
    """
    if path is None:
        path = get_settings().db_path
    if str(path) != ":memory:":
        Path(path).parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    conn = sqlite3.connect(path, isolation_level=None, check_same_thread=False)
    conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row
    conn.enable_load_extension(True)
    sqlite_vec.load(conn)
    conn.enable_load_extension(False)
    conn.execute("PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL")
    conn.execute("PRAGMA busy_timeout=10000")
    conn.execute("PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON")
    conn.executescript(SCHEMA)
    _migrate(conn)
    return conn


# Columns added after a table was first created: (table, column, definition). CREATE IF NOT EXISTS
# doesn't add them to an existing DB.
MIGRATIONS = [
    ("signal", "llm_usage_id", "INTEGER REFERENCES llm_usage(id)"),
    ("verbatim_extraction", "recheck_llm_usage_id", "INTEGER REFERENCES llm_usage(id)"),
    ("signal", "support_question", "INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0"),   # Q-020, D-024
    # Simulated ingest waves (Q-012, D-027): the wave in which an item becomes visible to the pipeline.
    ("source_item", "wave", "INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1"),
    ("finding", "source_kind", "TEXT"),            # verbatim | study | web | reference
    ("finding", "polarity", "TEXT"),               # pain | want | like | context
    ("finding", "category", "TEXT"),
    ("finding", "first_wave", "INTEGER"),
    ("requirement", "effort", "TEXT"),             # S | M | L rough effort (prioritization only, no cost math)
    ("requirement", "must_not_lose", "INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0"),
    ("requirement", "realization_note", "TEXT"),
    ("requirement", "created_by", "TEXT"),
    ("requirement", "first_run_id", "INTEGER"),
    ("requirement", "derivation_json", "TEXT"),     # raw AI draft incl. horizon_reason, cited IDs
    ("requirement_target", "evidence_level", "TEXT"),
    ("requirement_target", "proposed_priority", "TEXT"),   # AI proposal; `priority` is the PM-confirmed one
    ("requirement_target", "run_id", "INTEGER"),
    ("change_proposal", "kind", "TEXT"),            # priority | status | content | new_requirement | link_finding
    ("audit_event", "run_id", "INTEGER"),
    # Curated reference layer: provenance + competitor details per model (competes_with, markets, strengths).
    ("vehicle_model", "source_ids_json", "TEXT"),
    ("vehicle_model", "profile_json", "TEXT"),
    # plan-v2 (D-040+): where a requirement came from and whom it serves
    ("requirement", "origin", "TEXT"),             # primary trigger lane (see candidate.origin)
    ("requirement", "origin_mix_json", "TEXT"),    # evidence share per lane, computed from linked findings
    ("requirement", "personas_json", "TEXT"),      # customer groups served
    ("requirement", "candidate_id", "TEXT"),
]


def _migrate(conn: sqlite3.Connection) -> None:
    for table, column, definition in MIGRATIONS:
        cols = {r["name"] for r in conn.execute(f"PRAGMA table_info({table})")}
        if column not in cols:
            conn.execute(f"ALTER TABLE {table} ADD COLUMN {column} {definition}")
            if (table, column) == ("signal", "llm_usage_id"):
                # Backfill: until D-023 every signal came from its verbatim's first-pass call.
                conn.execute(
                    """UPDATE signal SET llm_usage_id = (SELECT e.llm_usage_id FROM verbatim_extraction e
                       WHERE e.source_item_id = signal.source_item_id AND e.extractor_version = signal.extractor_version)"""
                )

